Implement only the phase ID named in my next message. Follow the execution order and dependency rules in section 18, including lettered phases. Preserve already accepted behavior.
Read the whole relevant system section before coding. Do not invent additional systems.
Separate pure simulation from the KSP adapter. One authoritative simulation owns all colony inventory.
Verify every KSP API you use against the local target installation or current primary documentation.
Record verified signatures and runtime observations in DECISIONS.md.
Do not use Harmony or require Module Manager. Do not copy other mods' source or Squad assets.
Before edits, list the phase scope, normative sections, dependencies, interfaces and acceptance cases. Implement a complete vertical slice of that phase, not unrelated future features.
Run the phase's automated tests. Perform its game checks only if KSP is actually available.
